# Content Machine governance rule

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` and `docs/GO_NO_GO_DECISION.md` before changing anything. `docs/DOCUMENT_OWNERSHIP_MAP.md` lists which documents are current; documents marked historical (Stage 0 charter and plan, recovery records, Replit notes) describe past states and must not be followed as instructions.

The product closeout is implemented and verified. Do not reopen completed work or start a new product cycle. Production is blocked only on the owner creating the Render environment; never create paid resources, change billing or handle production secrets.

Work on a dedicated branch, open a focused pull request, keep `CI` green, never weaken tests, typecheck, authentication, ownership checks, database guards, secret scanning or the accessibility gate, and never invent evidence. Follow `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` for any UI change. Update `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` when the operational state changes.
